  "id": "Compound::DB00712 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Flurbiprofen, a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory compound, is linked to Slc22a6 through a series of molecular interactions that involve both direct and indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Flurbiprofen, through its inclusion in the class of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs, binds to Slc22a6, a transporter involved in the uptake of various compounds. This binding is supported by the lowest common ancestor relationship between Flurbiprofen and Piroxicam, both of which are classified as organooxygen compounds, and their shared dependence on the enzyme inhibitor category. Additionally, Flurbiprofen's ability to cause fever chills and white blood cell abnormalities, which are mediated by Cidofovir and Foscarnet, respectively, further reinforces the notion that Flurbiprofen interacts with Slc22a6 through a mechanism involving transporter activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Slc22a6 in the cellular uptake of Flurbiprofen and its metabolites, suggesting a broader functional relationship that spans multiple pharmacological effects.",
